Diagnosis: the 7 failures are all semantic, not syntactic — (a) fan-out joins that duplicate entities before projection/aggregation (`sp0536`, `sp0547`, `sp0766`), (b) negation applied as a row-level `!=`/flag filter instead of entity exclusion (`sp0765`, `sp0766`), (c) under-specified projection where gold returns full joined rows (`sp0755`), and (d) an empty result wrongly "repaired" into a non-empty one (`sp0786`). The current prompt actively pushes toward DISTINCT-on-names and treats every empty result as a bug. I add generic join-cardinality/negation/projection rules, make the repair turn re-read the question with concrete execution evidence, and stop forcing a rewrite when a query legitimately returns zero rows (instead verifying its literals locally).

